[{"sha":"7cbcec1a9818c525734a6f70fb655bcc0c39cdc7","node_id":"C_kwDOEFLz89oAKDdjYmNlYzFhOTgxOGM1MjU3MzRhNmY3MGZiNjU1YmNjMGMzOWNkYzc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/7cbcec1a9818c525734a6f70fb655bcc0c39cdc7","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/7cbcec1a9818c525734a6f70fb655bcc0c39cdc7","author":{"name":"Igor Serganov","email":"iserganov@tunein.com","date":"2026-10-09T17:05:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"Igor Serganov","email":"iserganov@tunein.com","date":"2026-10-09T17:05:42Z"},"tree":{"sha":"569780682fd369b3b973402ffee88932dd0ef503","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/trees/569780682fd369b3b973402ffee88932dd0ef503"},"message":"hscontrol: arm ephemeral GC when a node registers with an auth key\n\nThe ephemeral garbage collector was only armed when a long-poll\nsession ended, or for every ephemeral node at startup. A client that\nregistered and went away before its first long-poll reached Connect,\nfor example a pod killed right after login, never ended a session,\nso no deletion timer was armed. The node then stayed until headscale\nrestarted, well past node.ephemeral.inactivity_timeout.\n\nSchedule the GC right after a successful auth-key registration. The\nexisting Cancel in serveLongPoll stops the timer once the node\nconnects. A timer that fires while a session is live is still skipped\nby the ActiveSessions check.\n\nTestEphemeralGCDoesNotDeleteReconnectedNode now cancels the\nregistration timer before replaying its sessions. Otherwise the 50ms\ntimer could fire while the test's Connect was still waiting for a\nNodeStore flush.","parents":[{"sha":"519b4621f3a99fd9cc446352d94a9f38e0a0b97f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/519b4621f3a99fd9cc446352d94a9f38e0a0b97f","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/519b4621f3a99fd9cc446352d94a9f38e0a0b97f"}],"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_